menu "USB GPIO Extender"

    config USBGPIO_WIFI_SSID
        string "WiFi SSID"
        default ""
        help
            SSID of the WiFi network to join. Leave blank to disable WiFi
            entirely - the firmware still works as a plain USB GPIO
            extender either way; WiFi only adds a read-only status page
            and a status LED, never a second control path.

            Set via "idf.py menuconfig", not by editing this default: real
            credentials belong in your local sdkconfig, which is
            gitignored. Never put a real SSID/password here or in
            sdkconfig.defaults - both are committed to a public repo.

    config USBGPIO_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "WiFi password"
        default ""
        help
            WPA2 password for USBGPIO_WIFI_SSID. Same rule as above: set
            via menuconfig, never commit a real value.

    config USBGPIO_MDNS_HOSTNAME
        string "mDNS hostname"
        default "esp32"
        help
            Once connected to WiFi, the board is reachable at
            <this>.local (default: esp32.local) for the status page.

endmenu
